# Scripts shipped to and executed on Linux (Brown Oscar) MUST keep LF line
# endings. This overrides a Windows checkout's core.autocrlf=true, which would
# otherwise convert them to CRLF and break bash on the cluster (e.g.
# COLLOID_ENV_READY=1\r != 1, or `conda activate colloid\r` not found).
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.slurm text eol=lf
